"page": 1, "unit_id": "ADD-03:2.5", "words": "Applications for a Shutdown Acceptance Letter shall be made to the Network Operator not later than eight (8) Working Days before the Proposal Due Date."}], "id": "S2", "kind": "fact", "text": "The cover summary describes the tie-in shutdown application as for the Authority's acceptance, made within eight Working Days of the date of the Addendum; operative clause 2.5 requires a Network Operator letter, applied for not later than eight Working Days before the Proposal Due Date."}, {"evidence": [{"doc": "ADD-03", "kind": "span", "page": 1, "unit_id": "ADD-03:cover/para3", "words": "with no cure period and with no deduction during the Ramp-Up Period"}, {"doc": "ADD-03", "kind": "span", "page": 2, "unit_id": "ADD-03:5.2", "words": "‘No cure period applies to an event under Clause 31.1(b) or Clause 31.1(d).’ is substituted."}], "id": "S3", "kind": "fact", "text": "The cover summary says the new Unavailability Event has no deduction during the Ramp-Up Period; operative clauses 5.1 and 5.2 add event (d) and a no-cure-period rule but no Ramp-Up provision was found in ADD-03 by search."}, {"id": "S4", "kind": "interpretation", "text": "The cover summary is descriptive; the changes it lists are made by the operative provisions (Sections 2-5, Appendix A), which are answered in other batches. Its only own effect is the Form 4-A acknowledgement obligation."}, {"id": "S5", "kind": "interpretation", "text": "Clause 1.2 is an interpretation rule matching how ops are applied (targets read at stage ADD-02); it amends no unit."}]}, "run_id": "ADD-03-host-20261005T173952Z-d69e", "ts": "2026-10-05T17:39:52Z"}
